+# Adversarial exchange — Astra — 20260906T1435Z
+
+**Decision: REDESIGN the Laurent screen; CONTINUE two bounded D125 gates; STOP further elimination expansion for now. Systems: UPGRADE deadline execution within the existing trial.** No unrestricted new mechanism emerges. Scope and theorem hypotheses determine these decisions, independently of model agreement.
+
+This is cross exchange, not another blind scan. I read all four submissions whole, then the nine charged interface/gate reports whole, packet, collection, FALLACY and Strinz ledger. Rehashed packet and four submissions match collection. All blind reports finished by 15:02:41; collection was verified at 21:26:31 after the coordinator gap. Their prior hash-pinning remains intact. Post-cutoff confirmations below are separate deltas, never retroactive blind evidence. All local references below mean immutable basenames under `/tmp/jc2-lane.6X3qUe/inputs`; “GGV” means `core-ggv-layout.txt`.
+
+**The Laurent-count objection is correct, but does not destroy the receiver screen.** In `L^(l)=K[t^(±1/l),pi]`, the weight equation `rho*a+sigma*b=rho+sigma`, with `b>=0`, does not bound b because a can be negative. At `(rho,sigma)=(1,1)`, `t^(2-b)pi^b` exists for every integer `b>=0`. This refutes Fable’s finite ambient-monomial enumeration and its derivation of a uniform root bound from that enumeration. It does not show that these monomials can be Euler elements for a specified face, refute Proposition 2.11, or establish receiver nonexistence. GGV’s ring definition is at 129–140; Theorem 2.6 and Proposition 2.11 are at 366–392 and 420–441.
+
+There is an exact **source-specific repair**, directly from Theorem 2.6(2),(3). For polynomial receivers with `[P,Q]=c*gamma^k`, set `l=k+1`, `t=gamma^l`. Then `barP,barQ` belong to `K[t^(1/l),pi]` and have bracket `c/l`. Choose a positive transformed direction `(rho,sigma)` and put `d=v(barP)>0`, `w=rho+sigma`. Each endpoint of the theorem’s homogeneous Euler element F is either `(1,1)` or `(w/d)` times the corresponding endpoint of barP: alignment and equal weights fix that positive scalar. Both alternatives have nonnegative coordinates. Every support point of F lies between its endpoints, so F has no negative t-exponents. Therefore
+
+`deg_pi(F) <= floor((rho+sigma)/sigma)`.
+
+In Proposition 2.11’s notation `F=t^a*pi^v*f(z)`, `ell(barP)=t^c*pi^s*p(z)`, with `f(0)p(0)!=0`, every distinct root of p divides separable f. Thus their number is at most `deg(f)<=deg_pi(F)`, giving at most two at transformed `(1,1)`, equivalently original `(1,l)`. If counting the extra axis root from `pi^s`, then `s>0` forces `v>0` by the start-endpoint clause, reserving its place in the same bound. This repairs the application using source polynomiality and endpoint geometry; the bare Laurent argument stays refuted. No ordinary-polynomial-in-t clause was imported. [GGV:164–180, 370–374, 420–464.]
+
+The remaining endpoint prohibition is real: Theorem 2.6(4) excludes original endpoints `(i,j)` with `i=l*j` whenever the transported positivity hypotheses hold. Proposition 2.11(2) also survives, but concerns **F’s** endpoint separation. Fable’s statement that monomial faces are automatically consistent is too broad: Remark 2.5 says monomial F forces monomial leading P when the weight sum is nonzero; it does not exempt a diagonal monomial P from clause (4). [GGV:364–374, 3271–3294.]
+
+There is a recorded licensed receiver class: `monomial-jacobian-euler-interface-astra-20260906.md:16–37` consumes the accepted forward descent from the M2=105 parent to `(25,15;21,2;k=2)`, in `K[gamma,pi]` with bracket `c*gamma^2`. Correct constantization therefore gives a necessary endpoint client at that inherited license tier. The stopped inversion/ordinary-Euler port remains stopped. The actual row gate, Moh primary text and forced faces are absent here; targeted retrieval did not obtain Moh’s theorem text. Consequently no newly checked forced-face violation, exhaustive receiver basis, K7 cut or ray exclusion is available. Client applicability and a discriminating forced face are separate requirements. A failed chosen reverse lift would likewise not prove that a chart point has no other lift; Fable’s proposed acceptance lifter needs a proved reconstruction map first.
+
+**Astra’s restricted-pole card:** I find no theorem-hypothesis mismatch in the blind formulation as written. It uses `R=ell(P)`, the corrected Puiseux map, positive directions and the twisted equation `[E,R]=gamma^k*R`. If the least gamma term of R is `gamma^s*r(pi)`, with `s>=0`, `deg(r)>0`, a negative least exponent u in E produces coefficient `u*e*r'-s*e'*r`; its highest pi coefficient is nonzero because `u*deg(r)-s*deg(e)<0`. Its gamma order cannot occur on the right. For a nonmonomial positive-direction polynomial face the required positive pi-degree is present. The mixed-start restriction for `sigma>(k+1)rho` is consistent with this argument. The endpoint repair above already supplies the needed polynomiality. This same-model audit **does not promote Astra’s lemma or support cuts**. One genuine notation mismatch is in the earlier interface report at line 94: the theorem licenses a bracket against the leading form, not full P. The blind card avoids it. [GGV:366–374; Astra blind, Card 2.]
+
+**Degree 125: conditional arithmetic improves; the reduction remains OPEN.** The primary [GGHV algorithm tables, §§5–6](https://arxiv.org/html/1708.07936v1#S5) give F2’s `(A0,A0',A1)=((5,20),(1,0),(7/5,2))` and `(m,n)=(3,5)` at 125. For a standard pair with that starting triple, its type-II.b Euler endpoint aligns with A0. At `(5,-1)`, Euler weight is 4 and A0 weight is 5, so `p/q=4/5`, hence `q=5`; after swapping, the endpoint is `(16,4)=(4/5)(20,5)`. This derives q from weights, not from the denominator of A1. [GGV:1522–1587, 2116–2136.]
+
+If Corollary 7.4 reaches the predecessor of that swapped polynomial pair, it gives `ell(P)=R^(5m)` and `en(R)=(4,1)`. Polynomiality of the power forces R’s least x-valuation nonnegative. Nonmonomiality and height one then force `R=a*x^4*y+b*x^c`, with `a*b!=0`. Positive weight and a direction strictly between `(0,-1)` and `(1,-1)` give `0<c<3`; thus `c=1,2` and directions `(1,-3),(1,-2)`. This is conditional first-face arithmetic, not a polygon classification. Fable’s prospective “open family at b=5” describes the wrong height after the proposed power extraction.
+
+The unresolved antecedent is Corollary 7.4’s positivity interval and valuation/endpoint transport, followed by all later Laurent shears and opposite-vertex arguments. [GGV:2074–2109.] The [lower-polygon paper, Corollary 1.6 and Propositions 2.1–2.2/3.12](https://arxiv.org/html/1605.09430v2#S2) was checked directly: its continuing §2 assumption resets to an `(m,n)`-pair, but its positivity proof retains van den Essen dependencies. GGHV 2022 Proposition 4.3 concerns `(8,28)` specifically, with q=4 and height two; substitution of numbers is not an application of that theorem. Its §2 list is strictly sub-125. Neither Strinz’s existential standardization nor the confirmed Roy contract supplies the unconstructed standard-pair-to-carrier map. A necessary polygon system’s solution would still require reconstruction. [Frozen GGHV:94–126, 492–618; Strinz ledger, non-composition statement.]
+
+**Deduplication and ranking**, by target/mechanism/object/test:
+
+| Fingerprint | Disposition |
+|---|---|
+| Receiver exclusion / corrected Euler endpoints / source-derived polynomial faces / forced-face test | REDESIGN Fable’s count; bank repaired restriction, require actual face data before a cut. Astra’s pole argument overlaps this implication. |
+| D125 source intake / coordinate transport / complete guarded ordinary-J ideal / literal-row gate | Coordinator and Sol substantially coincide; post-cutoff contract and normalization confirmations discharge their earlier desk dependencies. |
+| D125 elimination / terminal-face filtration / full Q-linear map / diagonal-rank test | Distinct Astra proposal, still unpromoted; further expansion deferred. |
+| Standard F2 restriction / published chain / necessary polygon images / interval and vertex gate | Fable’s distinct, bounded theorem opportunity; redesign around actual missing arrows. |
+| D108 / axis shear and positivity / already retired family / dependency audit | Sol’s distinct proof-debt reduction, low global marginal value; park, never reopen compute. |
+
+Strongest **proof attack** remains a uniform obstruction to source-compatible global polynomial realizability. Corrected receiver endpoints are a cheap necessary screen, not that obstruction. K16’s simultaneous full-product target, separate b=0 boundary and both factors of `3d²=m` remain the structural target; repeating the charged ramification/square no-gains contributes nothing. Strongest **CE attack** is the complete guarded original polynomial-source D125 contract. Its missing mathematical outcome is characteristic-zero nonemptiness; neither local carrier survivors nor a necessary polygon solution substitutes for it.
+
+**Post-cutoff composition.** Consume the different-model source-contract confirmation at original-source scope and the Fable normalization confirmation with the stated root31 normal/optimized checks and earlier153 controls. The original/transformed coefficient presentations have the confirmed fixed-rational ideal equality. The triangular normalization has only characteristic-zero field-point/nonemptiness equivalence, not ideal equality, scheme isomorphism or mod-p equivalence. Counts `571+1551` are raw coordinates before jets/pins. The terminal exporter preflight retains every row and the degree guard; root report/transaction/pins were checked, code review remains pending, and no production/import/solver run occurred. These are local interface gains under the active trial, not a global scope reversal.
+
+Astra’s `596` small blocks, `1760` columns and maximum `6x5` concern the original associated graded object. The supplied diagonal script, read whole but not run here, constructs neither the full source Taylor bases with tails nor an inverse and substituted remaining rows. Small rank blocks measure neither fill nor runtime. Confirmed normalization does not turn that old count into the normalized dimension. Any later elimination must separately preserve the two target gauges, including the transformed constant coefficient rather than `Q(0,0)`. [Astra blind, Card 1; `astra_diagonal.py:16–114`; exporter preflight.]
+
+Only these two cards receive launch priority:
+
+1. **Standard-F2 interval/vertex gate — CONTINUE, redesigned.** Dependency: exact standard starting triple at its retained reduction tier, GGV Corollary 7.4/Theorem 7.6, proved positivity interval, and each subsequent coordinate map. Cheapest discriminator: one bounded desk pass proving the predecessor transport, then resolving the two height-one branches through the opposite-vertex step. Outcome: a licensed necessary polygon presentation or a named first missing arrow. Stop at the first unsupported interval, vertex or reconstruction claim; no system expansion or solve. This can change the theorem target, but cannot trim Roy coefficients without another source arrow.
+
+2. **Complete-source exporter code gate — CONTINUE before elimination expansion.** Dependency: confirmed full contract and characteristic-zero normalization, plus the pending implementation review. Check exact variable map, original jet/pin indexing, complete coefficient envelope, retained constant target, guard, zero rows and strict completion. Outcome: defect requiring repair, or eligibility for a separately authorized capped complete export/replay measuring actual size and cost. The exporter’s verifier reuses its formula, so replay alone is not an independent builder. Stop at preflight here: no production, import or solver. Use the prepared exporter; no new adapter. This work need not wait for Card 1.
+
+**Systems UPGRADE:** coordinator execution missed collection 15:25, exchange 15:50, synthesis 16:10 and close 16:35 despite timely peer completion. The collection/monitor gap defeats the blind reports’ earlier NO_CHANGE rationale. Within the existing 48-hour trial, overdue collection and deadline checks should take precedence over routine ideation on resumption; before another idle interval, complete the due handoff or obtain explicit human coverage. No durable assistant wake is exposed or assumed. Preserve the last completed-full-round clock, 12:39:13, until actual completion. Fable’s proposed shared AST scanner does not address this failure and is unnecessary for activity; existing normal/optimized controls are the relevant local evidence. No ledger, launcher or adapter change follows.
+
+CONTINUE K7 untouched: `.73` reported live at 21:24, original 70GiB/job and 20h caps, harvest September 7 about 04:30. STOP 99/D108 frontier compute, duplicate K16 square work and the covered graph/projection search. REDESIGN receiver work around licensed source faces. No broad sweep or coverage-clock reset occurred.
+
+Read primary: GGV definitions/endpoints, Proposition 2.1, Lemma 2.2, Theorem 2.6/proof/notes, Proposition 2.11/proof, Proposition 6.1, Corollary 7.4/Theorem 7.6; GGHV §2/whole Proposition 4.3; Roy source/jet/layer/payload core. Targeted web scope was the two primary papers linked above and unsuccessful Moh retrieval. Unread dependencies: Moh primary/actual receiver face artifacts, Joseph’s upstream lemma, van den Essen proofs, Strinz’s reduction bundle, complete census proofs, later D125 vertex/reconstruction arguments, exporter implementation and giant external certificates. Three same-model source assistants corroborated bounded readings; no different-model promotion results. No mathematical script or classifier was executed. No point, unit, properness, global125 theorem or JC2 solution is claimed.

